# Completion from the type checker, and the signature beside the line.
Shot completion
Alt a struct type declared, then a composite literal of it begun, with the first field not yet set offered as ghost text after the cursor
Also completion-hint a call to strings.Repeat typed as far as its second argument, with the signature shown beside the line and the parameter being typed in brackets
Caption Completion comes from the type checker: a struct you declared two lines ago completes its own fields, and a call shows its signature as you type.
Headline Completion from the type checker
Grid 80x12
Line type Point struct{ X, Y int }
Type "p := Point{"
Wait Prompt
Screenshot
Ctrl c
Wait Prompt
Type `strings.Repeat("ab", `
Wait Prompt
Screenshot completion-hint
